import hashlib,json
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;F=P.parent;R=F.parents[2]
sha=lambda b:hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()
packages=['real-data-pilot-chunk-durability-candidate01-2026-10-06','real-data-pilot-control-history-candidate01-2026-10-06']
evidence={};sources={};manifests={}
for name in packages:
 d=F/name;m=d/'MANIFEST01.json';manifests[name]=sha(m.read_bytes());evidence[str(m.relative_to(R))]=sha(m.read_bytes())
 for f in sorted((d/'candidate').glob('*.py')):sources[str(f.relative_to(R))]=sha(f.read_bytes())
 for n in ('REPORT01.md','INVERSE01.json'):
  f=d/n;evidence[str(f.relative_to(R))]=sha(f.read_bytes())
for n in ('DURABILITY_CHECK01.json','HISTORY_CHECK01.json','check_durability01.py','check_history01.py'):
 f=P/n;evidence[str(f.relative_to(R))]=sha(f.read_bytes())
review={'schema_version':1,'decision':'accepted','scope':'Independent combined changed-source review only; selected genuine archive schema2 route, optional chunk durability and control-history encoding. No empirical admission, concrete policy release, source integration, throughput or capacity acceptance.','candidate_manifests':manifests,'candidate_sources':sources,'evidence':evidence,'material_findings':[], 'verification':{'durability_tool':'8b9c47 exit0; automatic threshold fsync failure preserves exact primary, raw partial, unchanged durable watermark, terminal refusal and descriptor cleanup','history_tool':'68ebc1 exit0; five exact inverses, real Journal/Context._call zero-byte descriptor ordering, publication-failure retention, nonempty refusal and forced boundary audit','legacy_and_science':'Eleven exact baseline reconstructions in total; unchanged framing/f64 score bits, matching arithmetic, motif/sample/count/model/training definitions reused from accepted source evidence, not numerically rerun. Author byte/default/boundary controls inspected.'},'assumptions_and_limits':['Acknowledgement/readback in selected buffered PairLog/ScoreTail is not crash durability until a successful fsync barrier. Interval checks occur at writer activity; idle or blocked calls are not covered by a background timer. Watermarks are volatile, not restart authority.','Closed-history detection is sampled at the explicit policy interval/callback bound; mandatory binding/operation/ledger/context completion boundaries force full raw-byte audits. Current Run, Owner, source, native guard, captured held lease and spent counters remain checked. No writer exclusion or adversarial-write immunity is established. A slow audit can expire and stop execution.','Successful control/diagnostic original byte bodies and logical names are retained in durable hash-chained shards. Standalone successful control inodes are a declared storage-format change. Only verified zero-byte command staging is retired after its name/full stat including mode/empty hash descriptor is durably published; failed, nonempty and oversized records stop and remain. No remote recovery waiver applies to payload bytes.','Finite sharded retained controls remain separate from cumulative rounded network IO, payload/readback scratch, filesystem allocation, typed controls, original matrices and process memory. The illustrative 472000-command accounting is not a complete seven-graph reservation or measured fit.','Selected archive preflight eagerly imports archive_control_history and chunk_durability before the existing imported-authority snapshot. This review does not grant a nonarchive imported-lease route late-import exception. Final actual source closure and selected policy must bind installed helpers before activation.','No actual runtime throughput, power-loss restart, all-seven population, real feature/model capacity, strategy performance, fees/funding, returns or financial exposure claim was tested. Existing retention checkpoints may still impose frequent fsyncs; full history boundary cost remains workload dependent.'],'release_requirements':['Root must integrate exact accepted source composition, pin helper/source/runtime closure, explicitly register finite durability/history assumptions and complete physical/transport/control declarations, and obtain final concrete entry release before execution.','Do not reuse this source review as scientific/Owner/Binding, backup recovery, storage or native capacity evidence.']}
(P/'REVIEW01.json').write_text(json.dumps(review,indent=2,sort_keys=True)+'\n')
(P/'REPORT01.md').write_text('''# Combined overhead source review

Accepted the exact seven-module durability and six-file history/control candidates for source integration on the selected archive schema2 route. No material changed-seam defect was found. This is not approval of a concrete empirical policy, speed claim or resource fit.

Eleven literal baseline inverses preserve the old source outside the declared opt-ins. Original pair/tail encoding, f64 values, matching/scoring and scientific configuration remain unchanged. Independent focused checks passed: automatic fsync failure retains partial bytes and the exact primary error, leaves the durable watermark unchanged, refuses terminal success and closes descriptors; actual Context._call orchestration retains an empty staging file if durable descriptor publication fails, retires it only after successful journal publication, and refuses/retains nonempty staging. The history source and its five inverses were authenticated. These are mechanical fixtures, not genuine authority objects.

The durability policy explicitly separates acknowledged/read-back data from fsync-durable data. Its timer is checked at activity, not by a background flusher. Checkpoint, final and failure barriers remain. The history policy explicitly permits delayed detection of closed-evidence changes between full audits. Live Run/Owner/native/held authority and spent counters remain checked; binding, operation, ledger and Context completion force full byte audits. Slow full audits can expire. No exclusion of concurrent external writers is granted.

Successful original control bytes and names are retained in sharded chains with terminal anchors. Zero-byte staging retirement follows a durable original name/stat/mode/empty-hash descriptor. Failed, oversized and nonempty bytes remain. This changes successful-control storage layout; it does not erase payloads or assert current remote availability. Physical controls, cumulative network IO, scratch, filesystem allocation and RAM remain separate. The illustrative 472,000-command bounds (2,493,208,576 control bytes, 1,114,887,680 diagnostic bytes, 869 file slots) cover these domains only.

The joined archive preflight loads the selected new helpers before imported-authority snapshots. No nonarchive late-import exception is accepted. Root must install/pin the exact composition and bind finite policies and complete seven-graph resource declarations before any final entry release. Scientific/numerical proof is reused unchanged; no financial experiment, throughput benchmark, power-loss recovery or full-size capacity check was performed.
''')
members={}
for f in sorted(P.rglob('*')):
 if f.is_file() and f.name!='MANIFEST01.json':members[str(f.relative_to(P))]={'sha256':sha(f.read_bytes()),'bytes':f.stat().st_size}
(P/'MANIFEST01.json').write_text(json.dumps({'schema_version':1,'status':'SEALED_COMBINED_SOURCE_REVIEW_NOT_EMPIRICAL_RELEASE','members':members},indent=2,sort_keys=True)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'review_sha256':sha((P/'REVIEW01.json').read_bytes()),'manifest_sha256':sha((P/'MANIFEST01.json').read_bytes()),'candidate_manifests':manifests,'source_count':len(sources)}))
